 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Precision:** Depth values must be consistent in scale between rendered and prior maps.
-*   **Boundaries:** Pixels near image boundaries may have fewer neighbors; the KNN search should handle this gracefully (e.g., by returning fewer neighbors).
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If the prior depth map is noisy or inaccurate, the regularization may enforce incorrect structures.
+- If the external depth map is noisy, the KNN search might select incorrect neighbors, leading to inconsistent regularization [S1].
+- The choice of $m_{ar'}$ is critical; too small a value may penalize valid depth discontinuities, while too large a value may fail to enforce continuity [S1].
+- Precision issues may arise if depth values vary significantly in scale [G].
 
